  "response": "VERDICT\n\nThe current ACP contract (sections 16.3 and 16.4) is sufficiently precise to safely implement the proposed read-only POC. The contract structure provides the necessary machine-readable fields (authorization, capabilities, permitted_paths, constraints) to enable unambiguous execution and reporting.\n\nREQUIRED BEFORE POC\n\n* Define a lightweight, local schema validation mechanism to enforce the ACP envelope structure (16.3) at the POC execution lane interface, ensuring the POC strictly conforms to the protocol before any command is honored.\n* Explicitly define the POC-specific `permitted_paths` allow-list to ensure the execution lane is restricted to the necessary, minimal repository surface area for the read-only command.\n\nRECOMMENDED\n\n* Include a minimal `request_id` and `timestamp` in the ACP command envelope for the POC to exercise the correlation and tracking logic proposed in the target architecture.\n* Implement a simple structured parser in the POC execution lane that rejects any command containing unauthorized capabilities (anything other than `read_only` for this POC).\n\nOPTIONAL\n\n* Define a simple local logging mechanism within the POC execution lane to capture the ACP envelope content and the resulting execution report, simulating the auditable system proposed in the target architecture.\n\nNO CHANGE NEEDED\n\n* The core definitions in `ARCHITECTURE.md` (16.3, 16.4) require no changes to support this proof of concept.\n\nSMALLEST SAFE POC\n\n1.  **Command Construction**: Construct a JSON ACP command envelope strictly adhering to the fields in 16.3.\n2.  **Capability Enforcement**: Authorize only the `read_only` capability in the `authorization` field.\n3.  **Path Scoping**: Set `permitted_paths` to a restricted, read-only scope (e.g., `[\"services/\"]`).\n4.  **Kilo Receipt**: Simulate Kilo receipt by loading the JSON command into the execution lane's local context.\n5.  **Execution**: Kilo parses the envelope, validates the capability (`read_only`), enforces the path restriction, and executes a read-only shell command (e.g., `ls` or `git status`).\n6.  **Reporting**: Kilo produces a structured execution report (as defined in 16.3) detailing the outcome, status, verification performed, and any blockers.\n7.  **Isolation**: Ensure the POC runs entirely as a local, stand-alone node script without production dependency access, network calls, or interaction with Qwen/OpenClaw.",
